        "original_id": "52532bee-a822-5333-ae7c-b037402b286c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Cestrum, Bauhinia, Cestrum diurnum, Cestrum tomentosum\n- Taxonomy: Solanaceae, Fabaceae, Cercidoideae\n- Places: West Indies, Central America, South America\n\nFacts:\n- Cestrum is a genus of about 150 to 250 species of flowering plants in the family Solanaceae.\n- Bauhinia is a genus of more than 500 species of flowering plants in the subfamily Cercidoideae of the family Fabaceae.\n- Bauhinia has a pantropical distribution.\n- Cestrum diurnum, also called Din Ka Raja, is a species in the genus Cestrum that is native to the West Indies.\n- Cestrum tomentosum is a plant species in the genus Cestrum that ranges throughout Central America and South America.",
